From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:23:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: emulated USB devices' transfers on threads kept for them

nsyshid made a new thread for every asynchronous transfer and every
synchronous one (std::async). A game polls its Skylanders Portal of
Power or Disney Infinity Base many times a second, and making and ending
a thread for each poll ran the console's thread and memory budget down
until the app crashed. Each device now has two threads of its own, one
for its reads and one for its other transfers, which run them in the
order the game asks for them, as a real device answers them. Reads have
their own because an Infinity Base or Toypad read waits for the answer
to a write.

The portals' queues are also taken from under their locks: the Infinity
Base and the Toypad took their answers off their queues with no lock
while the command and figure threads added to them, and the Skylanders
portal took its figures' states under its query lock while a figure put
on or taken off changed them under its portal lock.
